{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>ואסף</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: ואסף המצורע, and ואסף נדחי ישראל. The metzora is likened to a dead person, and just as the ashes of the cow purify, so too the prayer of the righteous purifies as well. ואסף נדחי ישראל — in the future, as it is written: אז ידלג כאיל פסח. And they will not need the ashes of the cow, as it is written: בלע המות לנצח."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The three cited phrases correspond to Numbers 19:9, Leviticus 14:36, and Isaiah 27:13 respectively. The phrase אז ואסף את המצורע appears to conflate 'אז' from Isaiah 35:6 with the Leviticus citation; rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:34.938556160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}